  "worked_solution": "The rate at which the deer population $N(t)$ of the forest changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum deer population the forest can support and the current deer population. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-N),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum deer population the forest can support, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=150\\text{\u00a0deer},$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=k(150-N).\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
